{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A jar contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa9bc3e1ca566d171ec6b80e39ee4cc913b5aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> marbles, each of which is either red, yellow, or green. The ratio of the number of red marbles to the number of yellow marbles to the number of green marbles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/0730c958ff1d8a07b2313e89c17dbfb4412877c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7:3:5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> marbles of each colour are removed, the new ratio of the number of red marbles to the number of yellow marbles to number of green marbles is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67d6fb9ebda160961197f32a3f9bc87eb56724ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 5:1:3 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 15:7:11 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 13:5:9 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 9:5:7 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 209:89:149$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"703\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can let the number of red marbles initially be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d8dd5f375b5f3874868d24a8820fe854a68a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, the number of yellow marbles initially be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, and the number of green marbles initially be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> due to the ratio. Because the total number of marbles before marbles are removed was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa9bc3e1ca566d171ec6b80e39ee4cc913b5aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9243fc408b8f23d0deb80736bcd77a495409ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7x + 3x + 5x = 600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac530e1d07ed3a0b671baea54840a5e08eb1d459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15x = 600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c6848e489a3c07b3d856c14e2073a836f557671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{600}{15} = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This means that the number of red marbles initially was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/1694ae0324389c2a6f3b1a8f0cd1cd7757a60352.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times 40 = 280$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />, the number of yellow marbles initially was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03ec525ab96efe2808ffb8a576b03768a3db522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 40 = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />, and the number of green marbles initially was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c684474a4300940d7695d49d6ec5d2c0396a0b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 40 = 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> marbles are removed from each color, we see that the number of red marbles became <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5df17c7a6e3ced068c5501e1f76ded1675e9c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$280 - 20 = 260$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />, the number of yellow marbles became <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/5/f85ffd1dd9324b918fb36126c1b4052b22436ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 - 20 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />, and the number of green marbles became <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2440ce841a67fe410f7c6b48d7100650970a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200 - 20 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>The ratio is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/1387a23676f47baa8bbfac0dc87271761e40b20b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$260:100:180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"114\" height=\"14\" />. Simplifying the ratio, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ad242d0a0f8ea07366da71fff203ef0fef54600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 13:5:9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"115\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Pr